comments.body:
@RPRX I switched VLESS and VMess outbounds to the same `settings.multiplex` configuration. A positive `concurrency` enables the shared pool, and a positive `xudpConcurrency` enables a separate XUDP pool. If both are zero, traffic uses ordinary outbound connections.

I removed the old `mux` parser and the `SenderConfig.multiplex_settings` API path. Xray logs one warning when `mux` is present, including when both keys are present. The update removes 117 lines net compared with the previous PR commit and adds no files.

I tested old clients with new servers and new clients with old servers for both VLESS and VMess, with and without Multiplex. The API and Reverse checks passed, as did the Multiplex tests with `-race`.

@RPRX I followed your [`DispatchLink` approach](https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core/commit/56a45ad57893919bd43d7e764ab32bc5b1fb0c1e) and used the VLESS and VMess migrations as references ([#5076](https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core/pull/5076) and [#5143](https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core/pull/5143)). The layer that owns the connection handles its cleanup.

`proxyman` closes the application endpoints for ordinary VLESS and VMess, and Reverse closes its own endpoints. Multiplex finishes the logical sessions. This let me remove endpoint unwrapping and the duplicate cleanup pass from Multiplex.

The Multiplex implementation is 198 lines shorter, excluding tests. I verified interoperability in both directions with old and new builds.

@Meo597 补充一条规则：新收录的项目必须主要基于 Xray-core 构建核心体验，~~算是 https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core/pull/4718#issuecomment-2874659203 的进阶版，什么苹果~~

原因比如有些多内核的客户端中 Xray 只是选项之一，并不能促进 Xray 所倡导的理念即协议取舍与安全要求等，~~一键换核绕过~~

README 如果收录太多到了刷屏的地步其实就没意义了，有限的位置应当优先列出最契合 Xray 理念的项目，~~好钢用在刀刃上~~
